WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.410
Thank you very, very much.

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.250
Oh gosh.

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.580
It is, it's wonderful to be here.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.744
I was actually just in New York.

00:00:05.744 --> 00:00:09.368
You ever hail a cab just to
stop it from hitting you?

00:00:09.368 --> 00:00:11.870
(audience laughs)

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.387
Never know what to tip those guys.

00:00:13.387 --> 00:00:14.260
(audience laughs)

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.730
Big week in my apartment
building this week.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:16.730
Very big week.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:18.214
The phone book arrived.

00:00:18.214 --> 00:00:19.930
(audience laughs)

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.404
Yeah, thank god.

00:00:21.404 --> 00:00:23.210
(audience laughs)

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.324
I don't know how I was getting
by without the phone book.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:26.660
(audience laughs)

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.920
Open the door, it was staring
up at me from the floor like,

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.151
here, we printed a portion of the internet

00:00:31.151 --> 00:00:32.281
for you to throw away.

00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:35.114
(audience laughs)

00:00:38.261 --> 00:00:39.763
It's a lot of fun to tell jokes.

00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:42.010
(audience laughs)

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.913
I'm just so glad I'm not a magician.

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.060
(audience laughs)

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.100
Have you taken a moment today

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.000
to be grateful that you're not a magician?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:50.833
(audience laughs)

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:52.050
There's so much pressure.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.300
Comedy audiences come
out to have a good time.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.394
Magic is the only kind of entertainment

00:00:56.394 --> 00:01:00.777
where 90% of the crowd is trying
to ruin it for themselves.

00:01:00.777 --> 00:01:02.260
(audience laughs)

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.000
Go to a magic show just to see

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.407
if close-minded threatened
dudes just like, nope.

00:01:07.407 --> 00:01:08.750
(audience laughs)

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.980
No way, that ain't possible.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:11.909
Mirror.

00:01:11.909 --> 00:01:13.040
(audience laughs)

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.070
Some sort of mirror.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.673
You ain't sawing her in half.

00:01:15.673 --> 00:01:17.200
(audience laughs)

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.380
Like, yeah you did it.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.701
You proved what none of
us were trying to prove.

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:21.534
(audience laughs)

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.673
The boy onstage is not actually a wizard.

00:01:23.673 --> 00:01:25.330
(audience laughs)

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:26.250
And it's always dudes who,

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.583
mirror, no, no way.

00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:28.690
Girls are into it.

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.509
They're like, there is something more.

00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:31.720
(audience laughs)

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.020
That's how you should be.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.030
That's how I am, I love magic.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.476
Look at my friendly open face.

00:01:36.476 --> 00:01:37.309
(audience laughs)

00:01:37.309 --> 00:01:39.460
I sit in the front row, do I volunteer?

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.619
You're damn right I volunteer.

00:01:40.619 --> 00:01:42.320
(audience laughs)

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.020
A magician drops his fake thumb,

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.033
I didn't see nothin', I wanna believe.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.848
(audience laughs)

00:01:47.848 --> 00:01:50.130
I live in a non-magic world all day.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.159
Make it magic.

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:52.280
(audience laughs)

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.963
I was at a show recently
where I saw a man fly.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:56.950
Listen to me.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.210
I didn't misspeak.

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:01.626
A man, a wingless mammal took flight.

00:02:01.626 --> 00:02:02.810
(audience laughs)

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.392
You're not thinking,
imagine if I flew right now.

00:02:05.392 --> 00:02:06.225
(audience laughs)

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:07.620
If I could figure out
the muscle in my butt

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.281
that I need to flex, it's
working, and I just took off.

00:02:10.281 --> 00:02:11.114
(audience laughs)

00:02:11.114 --> 00:02:12.310
And I flew above the audience,

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.413
picked some of you up
with me, we flew around.

00:02:14.413 --> 00:02:15.246
(audience laughs)

00:02:15.246 --> 00:02:16.079
Best night of our lives.

00:02:16.079 --> 00:02:16.912
(audience laughs)

00:02:16.912 --> 00:02:17.830
And I saw this.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:21.110
And suddenly, I'm eight again
and I'm filled with majesty.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.230
And a guy next to me,
I don't know this guy,

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.410
who's this guy?

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.081
Leans over me and goes, it's a magnet.

00:02:27.081 --> 00:02:30.220
(audience laughs)

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.368
Magnet, he can't fly, magnet.

00:02:32.368 --> 00:02:34.994
(audience laughs)

00:02:34.994 --> 00:02:38.670
First of all, shut your
mouth and enjoy the show.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.704
Second of all, that explains nothing.

00:02:40.704 --> 00:02:41.701
(audience laughs)

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:42.570
What does that mean?

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.660
He stuffs his pocket with magnets?

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:45.850
The stage is a magnet?

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.167
That would look terrible.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.000
(audience laughs)

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.236
I think those are just two
things he doesn't understand.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.010
(audience laughs)

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:55.133
Like, I don't get magnets
and I don't get this.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.000
(audience laughs)

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.108
This is magnets.

00:02:58.108 --> 00:02:59.870
(audience laughs)

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.040
One time I had two pieces of
metal, they wouldn't touch,

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.330
then I flipped one, then they would.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.329
That's how he flies.

00:03:04.329 --> 00:03:07.207
(audience laughs)

00:03:07.207 --> 00:03:09.110
Must be very frustrating
too for the magician

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:10.840
'cause there's no noise to make

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.960
when you see a magic
trick for the audience.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.200
With comedy, it's very rewarding

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.358
'cause there's a built-in
biological response,

00:03:16.358 --> 00:03:17.660
which is laughter.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.190
But with magic there's nothing.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:20.460
You can see the best trick in the world,

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.133
whatever noise you make
sounds condescending and fake.

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:24.370
(audience laughs)

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.660
He can be like, okay
Pete what was you card?

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:26.493
You can tell me.

00:03:26.493 --> 00:03:27.420
Tell us now, what was your card?

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.156
It was the three of clubs, okay yeah.

00:03:29.156 --> 00:03:30.460
And you signed it?

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.413
Is that right, you signed it?

00:03:31.413 --> 00:03:32.910
Yeah, okay.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.145
And then you put it in this
barrel of fire, is that correct?

00:03:35.145 --> 00:03:36.270
(audience laughs)

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.020
We all watched as you placed
it in a barrel of fire, yeah.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.440
And the whole time I was blindfolded,

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.334
upside down in a tank of
water, is that correct?

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:44.210
(audience laughs)

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:45.911
Yeah, it's back, three of clubs.

00:03:45.911 --> 00:03:46.790
(audience laughs)

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:50.473
And now it's all on you and
you just have to be like ooh.

00:03:50.473 --> 00:03:53.306
(audience laughs)

00:03:54.313 --> 00:03:55.585
How?

00:03:55.585 --> 00:03:57.597
(audience laughs)

00:03:57.597 --> 00:03:59.277
Not what I expected.

00:03:59.277 --> 00:04:00.902
(audience laughs)

00:04:00.902 --> 00:04:01.735
It must suck.

00:04:01.735 --> 00:04:04.030
I bet it's the dream of
every magician in the world

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:05.190
that there would be some sort of

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:08.440
involuntary knee-jerk
response to seeing magic.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.756
That they would be like,
the tiger was over here.

00:04:10.756 --> 00:04:11.589
(air blows)

00:04:11.589 --> 00:04:12.422
Voila, it's over here.

00:04:12.422 --> 00:04:13.312
And people would just be like,

00:04:13.312 --> 00:04:14.835
(Pete screams)

00:04:14.835 --> 00:04:16.693
(audience laughs)

00:04:16.693 --> 00:04:18.308
(Pete screams)

00:04:18.308 --> 00:04:19.141
Oh magic.

00:04:21.108 --> 00:04:23.195
(audience claps)

00:04:23.195 --> 00:04:24.890
I love your magic.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.590
You don't wanna make this noise,

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.108
you have to make this noise.

00:04:28.108 --> 00:04:30.568
(Pete screams)

00:04:30.568 --> 00:04:32.030
(audience laughs)

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:33.740
Then there are people that
don't quite get the trick,

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:34.573
but they fake it.

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:35.423
They're like, oh yeah.

00:04:35.423 --> 00:04:36.371
(Pete moans)

00:04:36.371 --> 00:04:38.410
(audience laughs)

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.724
Magic.

00:04:39.724 --> 00:04:40.680
(audience laughs)

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.582
Oh the tiger moved.

00:04:41.582 --> 00:04:44.190
(Pete mumbles)

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.392
Thank you very, very much everybody.

00:04:45.392 --> 00:04:46.225
(audience cheers)

00:04:46.225 --> 00:04:49.392
You have a great night, appreciate it.

